{"id":"mcexam","name":"mcexam","aliases":[],"caption":"Create randomized Multiple Choice questions","authors":[{"id":"vannieuwenhuyze","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Jorre Vannieuwenhuyze","year":"2017"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"0.5","date":"2021-09-12"},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p>\n      This LaTeX package automatically randomly permutes\n      the order of questions as well as the answer options\n      in different versions of a multiple choice exam/test.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      Next to the exam versions themselves, the package also allows\n      printing a concept version of the exam,\n      a key table with the correct answers or points, and\n      a document with solutions and explanations per exam version.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      The package also allows writing an R code which processes\n      the results of the exam and calculates the grades. \n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      The following other LaTeX packages are required:\n      <ref refid=\"enumitem\">enumitem<\u002fref>,\n      <ref refid=\"environ\">environ<\u002fref>,\n      <ref refid=\"etoolbox\">etoolbox<\u002fref>,\n      <ref refid=\"longtable\">longtable<\u002fref>,\n      <ref refid=\"newfile\">newfile<\u002fref>,\n      <tt>pgffor<\u002ftt> (from the\n      <ref refid=\"pgf\">PGF/TikZ<\u002fref> bundle),\n      <ref refid=\"xkeyval\">xkeyval<\u002fref>, and\n      <ref refid=\"xstring\">xstring<\u002fref>.\n    <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/mcexam/README.md"},{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/mcexam/mcexam.pdf"}],"ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/mcexam","file":true},"miktex":"mcexam","texlive":"mcexam","topics":["random","exam"],"also":["esami"]}